1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,275
Power On & Loading.

2
00:00:02,225 --> 00:00:06,100
The correct startup sequence and how to load the Sunday scene.

3
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:10,175
Always turn on from SOURCE to SPEAKERS — speakers on LAST.

4
00:00:10,175 --> 00:00:13,762
This prevents the loud pop that damages speakers.

5
00:00:13,762 --> 00:00:15,712
Power-On Steps.

6
00:00:15,712 --> 00:00:22,662
Console & stage boxes first: Press power and wait for the X32 to fully boot — faders will motor to default.

7
00:00:22,662 --> 00:00:28,750
Wireless receivers & computers: Turn on mic receivers, playback, and livestream computers.

8
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:33,637
Bring mains down: Pull the Main LR fader all the way down or mute mains.

9
00:00:33,637 --> 00:00:38,212
Speakers and amps LAST: Turn on powered speakers and amplifiers.

10
00:00:38,212 --> 00:00:40,412
You'll hear nothing — good.

11
00:00:40,412 --> 00:00:45,725
Power OFF is the exact reverse: SPEAKERS off first, console off last.

12
00:00:45,725 --> 00:00:48,850
This protects your gear every single time.

13
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:51,162
Loading the Sunday Scene.

14
00:00:51,162 --> 00:00:55,475
Press VIEW in the Scenes section: The screen shows all saved scenes.

15
00:00:55,475 --> 00:01:02,837
Find your Sunday scene: Your sound lead will give you the scene number or name (fill it in here: ___).

16
00:01:02,837 --> 00:01:07,162
Press Go and confirm: Faders will motor to their saved positions.

17
00:01:07,162 --> 00:01:09,762
Watch them move — that's normal.

18
00:01:09,762 --> 00:01:14,300
Verify channel names: Each fader label should match what's plugged in.

19
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:17,462
If anything looks wrong, tell the sound lead.

20
00:01:17,462 --> 00:01:19,800
Line Check Before Service.

21
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:25,087
Wireless mics on: Check batteries are ≥50% charged.

22
00:01:25,087 --> 00:01:28,262
Fresh batteries every Sunday if possible.

23
00:01:28,262 --> 00:01:31,862
Test each mic: Speak into one mic at a time.

24
00:01:31,862 --> 00:01:34,712
Watch the meter and listen in the room.

25
00:01:34,712 --> 00:01:39,537
Walk-in music: Start background music at a low level as people arrive.

26
00:01:39,537 --> 00:01:44,825
Test stage monitors: Confirm each wedge or in-ear is working and playing the right mix.

27
00:01:44,825 --> 00:01:49,562
Mute unused channels: Start clean — only unmute channels as they're needed.

